The dataset is `data/processed/{{PKG_NAME}}.csv`: tidy long form, one row per observation. Every column is defined in [`docs/data-dictionary.md`](docs/data-dictionary.md), including its known caveats. [`data/processed/provenance.csv`](data/processed/provenance.csv) has one row per original file: where it came from, its sha256, the parser and tool versions that read it, and how clean the extraction was. Recipes for pandas, R and DuckDB are in [`docs/filter-pivot-recipes.md`](docs/filter-pivot-recipes.md).

## How to use it

### Python / pandas

```python
import pandas as pd

df = pd.read_csv("data/processed/{{PKG_NAME}}.csv", dtype=str)  # IDs keep their leading zeros
# Then convert the columns the dictionary declares numeric:
